{
  "platform_id": "UIsQ0jPhzJQ",
  "profile": {
    "video_id": "iron-snail:UIsQ0jPhzJQ",
    "purpose": "Tells the story of Fjällräven's founder and explains how the brand's Expedition Down Parka and Polar Expedition Parka are built. It draws on the creator's calls with Fjällräven's global product director and events manager.",
    "video_type": "explainer",
    "thesis": "Fjällräven's warmest parkas come from a founder who built gear through experimentation and collaboration. That history explains its offset-baffle down construction, synthetic insulation at the shoulders, and continued use of waxed G-1000 rather than the most technical, thinnest materials.",
    "key_takeaways": [
      "Fjällräven's founder started selling backpacks at 14, later used aluminium frames, and built the first Expedition jacket as two down jackets sewn together.",
      "The founder flew to the US to meet Eddie Bauer and learned how to sew a down jacket from George Lamb of Camp 7, at a time when outdoor gear makers shared knowledge openly.",
      "Down jackets can be built three ways: sewn-through, box baffle, or offset (double-layer) baffle construction. Fjällräven uses the offset method to remove cold spots.",
      "The Expedition Down Parka has synthetic insulation at the shoulders, placket and hood brim. Fjällräven says this is mainly to resist compression under backpack straps, with faster drying as a bonus.",
      "The Polar Expedition Parka adds a snow skirt, an inner neck baffle, large pulls for gloved hands, big side-entry and dump pockets, a synthetic fur hood ruff and G-1000 fabric.",
      "G-1000 began as a tent fabric that failed for being too heavy. Waxing it was inspired by skiers rubbing ski wax on their pants. Owners can wax it selectively, unlike an all-or-nothing Gore-Tex membrane.",
      "Fjällräven explains avoiding ultra-light technical fabrics this way: thinner gear raises cost and upkeep and makes failure more likely, which drives people away from the outdoors."
    ],
    "outline": [
      {
        "title": "The mad genius of Fjällräven",
        "summary": "Introduces the Fjällräven founder's backstory and the original Expedition jacket. Covers the hockey-lace cords and teases the synthetic shoulder padding.",
        "first_segment": 0,
        "last_segment": 1
      },
      {
        "title": "Undercover with the big wigs",
        "summary": "How the creator got the Expedition and Polar Expedition parkas and spoke with Fjällräven's global product director Donna and events manager Carl. Includes a no-payment disclaimer and a teaser of his question about why they still use wax.",
        "first_segment": 1,
        "last_segment": 4
      },
      {
        "title": "HelloFresh sponsorship",
        "summary": "Sponsor read for the HelloFresh meal kit.",
        "first_segment": 4,
        "last_segment": 5
      },
      {
        "title": "History of down jackets",
        "summary": "Covers Eddie Bauer popularising down jackets after WWII and nylon becoming available to civilians. Also covers the founder's dual-layer tent and his trip to the US, where George Lamb of Camp 7 taught him to sew a down jacket, set against the collaborative early outdoor industry.",
        "first_segment": 5,
        "last_segment": 9
      },
      {
        "title": "Jacket construction methods",
        "summary": "Explains sewn-through, box baffle and offset-channel construction, using strawberries as a prop. Says why Fjällräven's offset build is so warm and why the parka is sized to go over everything at base camp.",
        "first_segment": 9,
        "last_segment": 11
      },
      {
        "title": "Expedition parka features",
        "summary": "Covers the synthetic insulation at the shoulders, placket and hood, and Fjällräven's reasoning about backpack strap compression. Includes Donna's answer on whether synthetic padding loses loft.",
        "first_segment": 11,
        "last_segment": 14
      },
      {
        "title": "Polar Expedition Parka features",
        "summary": "A numbered rundown of the Polar Expedition Parka's features: snow skirt, neck baffle, large pulls, side-entry and dump pockets, synthetic fur hood, and G-1000 fabric.",
        "first_segment": 14,
        "last_segment": 15
      },
      {
        "title": "G-1000 and brand philosophy",
        "summary": "The origin of G-1000 and its wax treatment, and sustainability concerns about chemicals in waterproof membranes and zippers. Compares selective waxing with Gore-Tex, and gives Carl's explanation of why Fjällräven doesn't chase ultra-light technical materials.",
        "first_segment": 15,
        "last_segment": 20
      },
      {
        "title": "Push us, and a signed book",
        "summary": "Donna repeatedly asks viewers to push Fjällräven with feedback. A book arrives in the mail signed by the CEO.",
        "first_segment": 20,
        "last_segment": 21
      }
    ],
